HST Office: the Print page of the File panel ("Tệp tin" ▸ "In") shows the print settings and a live preview.

As in the reference suite, File ▸ Print (and Ctrl+P, the ribbon and menu Print) opens the Print page of the File
panel instead of the print dialog: settings on the left (big Print button with the copies, printer with
"Properties...", pages/range, the application's options such as Calc's "Thu phóng" scaling, print area and
Impress' slides/handouts/notes, paper sides, collate, orientation, paper size, pages per sheet), the preview of the
document on the right with page navigation and zoom (10–400 % of the real size, "Cả trang"), plus "Thiết lập trang"
(the application's page style dialog) and "Thêm tùy chọn" (the classic print dialog for the same job).

- vcl: PrintDialog has a second form, a panel (vcl/uiconfig/ui/hstprintpanel.ui, generated from printdialog.ui with
  the same widget ids plus the panel's own: moreoptions, pagesetup, previewscroll, zoomscale, zoomin, zoomout,
  zoomfit, zoomtext). Both forms share all code, so the options, preview and printout are the dialog's. The panel
  always previews, expands both sections and leaves the dialog's stored window state/preview/expander choices alone.
  takeSettings() carries the choices the job does not keep itself (printer/print to file, paper, orientation, sides,
  copies, collate, pages per sheet) between the forms.
- vcl::PrintJobPanel (include/vcl/hstprintjobpanel.hxx): Printer::PreparePrintJob offers a job with dialogs to a
  host (SetHost) where it would run the dialog; a host that takes it shows it in a PrintJobPanel. The job waits until
  Print() (Printer::ResumePrintJob: what PreparePrintJob does after the dialog's OK, then ExecutePrintJob and
  FinishPrintJob), RunClassicDialog() (OK prints; Cancel returns to the panel made again from the job) or
  Cancel()/destruction (Printer::CancelPrintJob: abortJob + FinishPrintJob, as the dialog's Cancel). Jobs without
  dialogs (API, direct), printers with their own dialog (macOS) and mail merge (PreparePrintJob without the
  hand-over flag) are unchanged.
- sfx2: the File panel is the host (InstallFileTabHandler registers it). The job's frame is the one whose view
  shell owns the job (SfxViewShell::GetPrinterController; with document tabs several frames share a window). A job
  of a Writer, Calc, Impress or Draw frame opens the panel on its Print page (BackstagePrintPage, hstbackstageprint.cxx); showing the page from its
  left-column item runs .uno:Print so the job comes back the same way. Leaving the page or closing the panel cancels
  the job; Ctrl+P inside the panel shows the page. The earlier "Print…" and "Print Preview" buttons of the page are
  hidden; "In hai mặt" (Writer) stays. The panel's size and place are BackstageWindow::GetPlacement's.
- solenv/sanitizers/ui/vcl.suppr: the print dialog's accessibility suppressions repeated for its panel copy, plus
  the zoom percentage label.
- Strings: vcl hstprintpanel.ui and sfx2 hstbackstage.ui "printwait"; Vietnamese in vcl/sfx2 messages.po (labels
  without an ellipsis, as the HST dialogs).

License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0); the new files are MPL-2.0.
Test: CppunitTest_vcl_hst_print_panel (panel lifecycle, hand-over); tests/unit/test_backstage_print.py.
